  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Multi-sectoral Humanitarian Response to Communities Severely Affected by the War in Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Targeting internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities in hard-to-reach areas of Central Darfur&#x2014;currently classified under IPC Phase 4 (Emergency) food insecurity&#x2014;and White Nile, one of the states hosting the largest IDP populations, this consortium project led by CAFOD and NCA aims to improve access to life-saving WASH, protection, and specialized GBV-related health services.

With a particular focus on vulnerable groups&#x2014;women, children, and people with disabilities&#x2014;the action will deliver clean water, appropriate sanitation facilities, hygiene support, GBV case management, psychosocial support, and community-based protection services. A crisis modifier component will enable rapid response to emerging needs, strengthening the initiative&#x2019;s adaptability in volatile contexts.

This response builds on prior successful collaborations with CAFOD and NCA. Local partners remain central to the delivery of community-led, sustainable solutions that reduce the strain on overstretched host communities while ensuring inclusive and impactful humanitarian outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
